Section 3 of the Evidence Act, in this Order referred to as the Act, is {a) by deleting the defmition of "document" and by substituting the new definition therefor - means any matter expressed, described or howsoever upon any substance, material, thing or article, including any matter embodied in a disc, tape, film, soundtrack or other device by means of - {a) letters, figures, marks, symbols, signals or other forms of description or representation whatsoever;

(b) any visual recording (whether of still or moving images);

(c) any sound recording or any electronic, magnetic, mechanical or other recording, whatsoever and howsoever made, or any electronic impulse or other data whatsoever;

(d) a recording or transmission of the means mentioned in (a}, (b) or (c), or by more than one of the means in paragraph (a), (b}, {c) or (d), intended to be used or which may be used for the purpose of expressing, or howsoever representing that matter; A writing is a document. Words printed, lithographed or photographed are documents. A map, plan, graph or sketch is a document. on wood, metal, stone or any other substance, material or thing is a document. A photograph or a negative is a document. A tape recording of a telephonic communication, including a recording of such communication transmitted over distance is a document. or other visual recording, including a recording of or other visual transmission over a distance is a document. A matter recorded, stored, processed, retrieved or produced by a is a document."; {b) by adding the following three new definitions'"'film" includes a microfilm and any negative; means any transparent material bearing a visual image in size either singly or as a series, and includes microfiche; means a transparent negative photograph on any substance or material, and includes any transparent negative photograph made from the original negative photograph.". of section 32.

Section 60 of the Act is amended, in subsection (3) -

(a) by deleting "other than" from the second line and by substituting "including" therefor;

(b) by inserting "or other document" immediately after 11thing" in the last line. of new section 60A.
